{"body":"Reading through this issue makes me think of DIDs in the more general sense.\n\nYou need a *stable identifier* that identifies the artifact: `did:<method>:<CID>`.\nYou want a way to verify the artifact(s): See the document property `verificationMethod`[^0][^1].\nYou want a way to discover the artifact(s): See the document property `service`[^0][^2].\n\nFor the `verificationMethod` you can use the `did:key` of the signing node(s).\n\nSo for me, this seems to boil down to thinking about some Radicle\nartifact DID method, how that can be resolved, and refining what goes\ninto the document.\n\n[^0]: https://www.w3.org/TR/did-1.0/#did-document-properties\n[^1]: https://www.w3.org/TR/did-1.0/#verification-methods\n[^2]: https://www.w3.org/TR/did-1.0/#services","replyTo":"b93d542a08d37bd80ad787550af998724b527f3c","type":"comment"}